Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below are the columns that matter for the requested report, together with the role each one will play and the key conditions that will connect the tables.

Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• web_region.id: primary‑key of a region – will be used to join to web_accounts.region_id.  
• web_region.name: printable “Region” needed in the final report.  

• web_accounts.id: primary‑key of an account – will be joined to web_orders.account_id.  
• web_accounts.region_id: foreign key that tells us in which region the account lives (join to web_region.id).  
• web_accounts.sales_rep_id: foreign key that tells us which sales rep owns the account (join to web_sales_reps.id).  

• web_sales_reps.id: primary‑key of a sales rep – join target for web_accounts.sales_rep_id.  
• web_sales_reps.name: human‑readable name of each sales rep – needed for the report.  
• web_sales_reps.region_id: sales rep’s “home” region (often the same as the accounts they own and can help in double‑checking joins).  

• web_orders.id: primary‑key of an order – used to count number of orders per region.  
• web_orders.account_id: foreign key that links an order to an account (join to web_accounts.id).  
• web_orders.total_amt_usd: dollar amount of each order – used to ❶ sum per region and ❷ sum per sales rep inside each region.  

Typical join / filter conditions  
1. web_region.id = web_accounts.region_id  
2. web_accounts.id = web_orders.account_id  
3. web_accounts.sales_rep_id = web_sales_reps.id  
4. All orders can be grouped by region (through the above joins).  
5. The “top rep” per region is obtained by comparing each rep’s SUM(total_amt_usd) against the MAX(total_amt_usd) for that region.  
6. To keep ties we select all reps whose total equals that MAX value.  

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory SQL queries (simple → complex → “almost final”)  
All are valid SQLite, use DISTINCT whenever useful, and are capped with LIMIT 20 so that you can peek at sample rows before running heavier queries.

```sql
-- 1. Show all region names that exist in the data set
SELECT DISTINCT "name"
FROM "web_region"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List a few accounts together with their region name
SELECT a."id"        AS "account_id",
       a."name"      AS "account_name",
       r."name"      AS "region_name"
FROM   "web_accounts"  AS a
JOIN   "web_region"    AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Peek at orders, already expanded to regions
SELECT o."id"            AS "order_id",
       o."account_id",
       r."name"          AS "region_name",
       o."total_amt_usd"
FROM   "web_orders"    AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts"  AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
JOIN   "web_region"    AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Which sales reps belong to which region?
SELECT DISTINCT sr."id"        AS "sales_rep_id",
                sr."name"      AS "sales_rep_name",
                r."name"       AS "region_name"
FROM   "web_sales_reps" AS sr
JOIN   "web_region"     AS r  ON r."id" = sr."region_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Total sales amount generated by each rep *inside each region*
SELECT sr."id"                AS "sales_rep_id",
       sr."name"              AS "sales_rep_name",
       r."name"               AS "region_name",
       SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS "total_sales_amt"
FROM   "web_orders"      AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts"    AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
JOIN   "web_sales_reps"  AS sr ON sr."id" = a."sales_rep_id"
JOIN   "web_region"      AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
GROUP  BY sr."id", r."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Region‑level summary: number of orders and overall sales
SELECT r."name"               AS "region_name",
       COUNT(o."id")          AS "num_orders",
       SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS "region_total_sales"
FROM   "web_orders"   AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts" AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
JOIN   "web_region"   AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
GROUP  BY r."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. For every region, what is the maximum sales amount posted by any single rep?
SELECT region_name,
       MAX(total_sales_amt) AS "max_sales_amt"
FROM (
      SELECT r."name"               AS region_name,
             SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS total_sales_amt
      FROM   "web_orders"      AS o
      JOIN   "web_accounts"    AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
      JOIN   "web_sales_reps"  AS sr ON sr."id" = a."sales_rep_id"
      JOIN   "web_region"      AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
      GROUP  BY sr."id", r."id"
) AS rep_tot
GROUP BY region_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. List ALL reps whose sales equal the max value in their region (ties kept)
SELECT tops."region_name",
       tops."sales_rep_name",
       tops."total_sales_amt"
FROM (
      SELECT r."name"               AS region_name,
             sr."name"              AS sales_rep_name,
             SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS total_sales_amt
      FROM   "web_orders"      AS o
      JOIN   "web_accounts"    AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
      JOIN   "web_sales_reps"  AS sr ON sr."id" = a."sales_rep_id"
      JOIN   "web_region"      AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
      GROUP  BY sr."id", r."id"
) AS tops
JOIN (
      SELECT region_name,
             MAX(total_sales_amt) AS max_sales_amt
      FROM  (
             SELECT r."name"               AS region_name,
                    sr."id",
                    SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS total_sales_amt
             FROM   "web_orders"      AS o
             JOIN   "web_accounts"    AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
             JOIN   "web_sales_reps"  AS sr ON sr."id" = a."sales_rep_id"
             JOIN   "web_region"      AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
             GROUP  BY sr."id", r."id"
      )
      GROUP BY region_name
) AS mx
  ON  mx.region_name   = tops.region_name
  AND mx.max_sales_amt = tops.total_sales_amt
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Join the region summary (query 6) with the top‑rep list (query 8)
SELECT reg."region_name",
       reg."num_orders",
       reg."region_total_sales",
       top."sales_rep_name",
       top."total_sales_amt"
FROM (
     /* Region summary */
     SELECT r."name"               AS region_name,
            COUNT(o."id")          AS num_orders,
            SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS region_total_sales
     FROM   "web_orders"   AS o
     JOIN   "web_accounts" AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
     JOIN   "web_region"   AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
     GROUP  BY r."id"
) AS reg
JOIN (
     /* Top reps per region with ties */
     SELECT tops."region_name",
            tops."sales_rep_name",
            tops."total_sales_amt"
     FROM   ( /* identical to query 8’s derived table */ 
             SELECT r."name"               AS region_name,
                    sr."name"              AS sales_rep_name,
                    SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS total_sales_amt
             FROM   "web_orders"      AS o
             JOIN   "web_accounts"    AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
             JOIN   "web_sales_reps"  AS sr ON sr."id" = a."sales_rep_id"
             JOIN   "web_region"      AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
             GROUP  BY sr."id", r."id"
     ) AS tops
     JOIN (
           SELECT region_name,
                  MAX(total_sales_amt) AS max_sales_amt
           FROM  (
                  SELECT r."name"               AS region_name,
                         sr."id",
                         SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS total_sales_amt
                  FROM   "web_orders"      AS o
                  JOIN   "web_accounts"    AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
                  JOIN   "web_sales_reps"  AS sr ON sr."id" = a."sales_rep_id"
                  JOIN   "web_region"      AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
                  GROUP  BY sr."id", r."id"
           )
           GROUP BY region_name
     ) AS mx
       ON mx.region_name   = tops.region_name
      AND mx.max_sales_amt = tops.total_sales_amt
)  AS top
  ON  top."region_name" = reg."region_name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. “Almost final” consolidated report: one row per region,
--     • number of orders,
--     • overall sales,
--     • *all* top‑rated rep names concatenated,
--     • their shared top‑sales amount.
SELECT rsum."region_name",
       rsum."num_orders",
       rsum."region_total_sales",
       treps."top_sales_reps",
       treps."top_sales_amount"
FROM (
      SELECT r."name"               AS region_name,
             COUNT(o."id")          AS num_orders,
             SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS region_total_sales
      FROM   "web_orders"   AS o
      JOIN   "web_accounts" AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
      JOIN   "web_region"   AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
      GROUP  BY r."id"
) AS rsum
JOIN (
      SELECT region_name,
             GROUP_CONCAT(sales_rep_name, ', ') AS top_sales_reps,
             MAX(total_sales_amt)              AS top_sales_amount
      FROM (
            SELECT r."name"               AS region_name,
                   sr."name"              AS sales_rep_name,
                   SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS total_sales_amt
            FROM   "web_orders"      AS o
            JOIN   "web_accounts"    AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
            JOIN   "web_sales_reps"  AS sr ON sr."id" = a."sales_rep_id"
            JOIN   "web_region"      AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
            GROUP  BY sr."id", r."id"
      ) AS rep_tot
      JOIN (
            SELECT region_name,
                   MAX(total_sales_amt) AS max_amt
            FROM (
                  SELECT r."name"               AS region_name,
                         sr."id",
                         SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS total_sales_amt
                  FROM   "web_orders"      AS o
                  JOIN   "web_accounts"    AS a  ON a."id" = o."account_id"
                  JOIN   "web_sales_reps"  AS sr ON sr."id" = a."sales_rep_id"
                  JOIN   "web_region"      AS r  ON r."id" = a."region_id"
                  GROUP  BY sr."id", r."id"
            )
            GROUP BY region_name
      ) AS mx
        ON  mx.region_name = rep_tot.region_name
       AND mx.max_amt      = rep_tot.total_sales_amt
      GROUP BY region_name
) AS treps
  ON treps."region_name" = rsum."region_name"
LIMIT 20;
```

